      "target": {
        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix: use Object.hasOwn instead of in operator in usage bar translator",
        "body": "Related: #98466\n\n## What Problem This Solves\n\n`key in table` checks the prototype chain, so `toString`/`constructor` keys match `Object.prototype` instead of falling through.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nReplace `key in table` with `Object.hasOwn(table, key)` (2 locations).\n\n## User Impact\n\nFixes incorrect usage bar rendering when keys coincide with prototype names.\n\n## Evidence\n\n**Runtime terminal proof:**\n\n![screenshot](https://github.com/zhangLei99586/openclaw/blob/proof-screenshots/pr-98139-proof.png?raw=true)\n\n- 15/15 tests passed + 2 new regression tests (`translator.test.ts`)",
        "branch": "fix/in-operator-prototype",
